    "_note": "K-EXAONE 2.0 (LG AI Research): 750B-A37B MoE upcycled from K-EXAONE 236B (3x capacity), 256K ctx, 10 languages, Apache 2.0. NEW model (DB had K-EXAONE 236B). Table 6 (Reasoning mode) 23 benches, own model only — competitor columns (K-EXAONE 236B, Qwen3.5 397B, GLM-5.1 754B, DeepSeek V4 Pro 1.6T; asterisks = official reports) 2nd-hand, skipped. Strengths: long-context retrieval (OpenAI-MRCR 94.4), Korean safety (KGC-Safety 99.8, ROK-Fortress 89.5 clearly best in table), agentic coding (SWE-Verified 68.2 / Terminal-Bench 2.1 43.8). 5 new benches (global_mmlu_lite, kgc_safety, rok_fortress, openai_mrcr, hmmt_feb_2026). FP8/NVFP4/DSpark are quantization variants of the same 750B model (same tech report) — not separate capability models, base only ingested. Multilingual per-language tables 7/8/9 (POLYMATH/GlobalMMLU-Lite/WMT24++) over-granular, aggregate used. S218b re-verify: release date corrected to 2026-07-31 (LG news); added 24-benchmark composite average (K-EXAONE 2.0 70.1 vs K-EXAONE 63.3, +10%). News confirms no new benchmark datasets + no separate quant-variant scores (FP8/NVFP4/DSpark = deployment/inference variants of base). DSpark speculative-decoding: E2E 1.27-1.77x, acceptance +32-66% vs MTP (inference efficiency, not capability)."
  },
